Human English claims that a Cartesian product of any number of injective spaces is injective in the product topology: project a map into the product onto the factors, extend each projected map, and reassemble the extensions. The AI English of `InjectiveSpace.pi` establishes that product injectivity: given an embedding and a continuous map into the product, each coordinate map extends along the embedding by injectivity of the corresponding factor, and the extensions reassemble to a map into the product that agrees with the original map because the coordinates agree. `proposition_1_3` is that same theorem. Checked: arbitrary index type matches "any number" of factors, and agreement of the extension is the pointwise identity of the coordinate extensions. **Theorem:** yes — products of injective spaces are injective. **Proof:** yes — project, extend each factor, reassemble.
